<title>ROMANIA: Romania posts Jan-April c/a deficit $282 mln.</title>
<headline>Romania posts Jan-April c/a deficit $282 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Romania's current account showed a $282 million deficit over January-April, sharply down from $698 million in the equivalent period of 1996, central bank preliminary data (BNR) showed on Monday.</p>
<p>				    JAN-APRIL 97	 JAN-APRIL 96</p>
<p> Current account (million USD)	-282		    -698</p>
<p> Trade balance			-230		    -609</p>
<p> Exports (FOB)		     2,617		   2,635</p>
<p> Imports (FOB)		     2,847		   3,244</p>
<p> Services balance		    -89		    -116</p>
<p> Income balance		     -108		    -101</p>
<p> Current transfers balance	 145		     128</p>
<p>NOTE: Romania's government plans to cut the current account deficit to $1.4 billion this year from an estimated $2.3 billion in 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
</text>
